<x-blog.callout label="What's included as standard">
    Every job covers interior and exterior glass, frames and sills wiped down, tracks cleared of sand and grit before the glass gets washed, a streak-free squeegee finish, and screens cleaned where they're removable. Accessible upper floors are handled with an extension pole system — jobs needing rope access or scaffolding get quoted separately with the right safety equipment.
</x-blog.callout>

<h2 class="text-2xl md:text-[28px] font-extrabold text-navy tracking-tight mt-12 mb-4">Why coastal windows need cleaning more often</h2>
<p class="text-muted text-[15.5px] leading-[1.85] mb-5">
    Salt-laden air leaves fine crystalline deposits on glass that attract moisture — left long enough, that combination can etch and permanently haze the surface rather than just sitting on top of it ready to be wiped away. In Bloubergstrand, Big Bay and Table View, the southeaster carries that salt (plus fine beach sand into window tracks) far more aggressively than suburbs even a few kilometres further inland. As a general guide, homes within a kilometre or two of the coast hold up better on a 2-4 week cleaning rhythm, while inland properties can usually stretch to monthly or every 6 weeks — with either schedule tightened up after a bout of strong wind or a southeaster storm.
</p>

